WEBVTT

00:20.862 --> 00:23.494
(TAKE ME AS I AM PLAYING)

00:31.841 --> 00:33.071
♪ I've been lookin' too hard ♪

00:33.106 --> 00:34.405
♪ For a home on the top ♪

00:34.441 --> 00:36.911
♪ On the top
 of the surface searchin' ♪

00:36.946 --> 00:38.541
♪ Lookin' for something deep ♪

00:38.576 --> 00:39.806
 ♪ Thought
 "It's too hard to reach" ♪

00:39.842 --> 00:42.213
♪ Never thought
 I was someone deservin' ♪

00:42.248 --> 00:43.813
♪ But it was all in my head ♪

00:43.848 --> 00:47.552
♪ Heavy weight on my chest
 only ever left me hurtin' ♪

00:47.587 --> 00:50.587
♪ Now I'm callin' a truce
 on the war in my mind ♪

00:50.622 --> 00:53.126
♪ 'Cause I'm finally learnin'
 I'm not ♪

00:53.162 --> 00:55.690
 ♪ Rollin' over, under
 inside out ♪

00:55.725 --> 00:58.495
 ♪ Turnin' myself
 all the way around ♪

00:58.530 --> 01:02.364
 ♪ What you see
 is what you get, so ♪

01:02.399 --> 01:06.233
♪ Baby, you can take me ♪

01:06.269 --> 01:12.246
♪ As I am ♪

01:13.147 --> 01:17.178
♪ Cause' I know I'ma take me ♪

01:17.214 --> 01:22.688
♪ As I am ♪

01:22.723 --> 01:25.559
 ♪ You can take it or leave it
 You can take it or leave it ♪

01:25.594 --> 01:27.723
(VOCALIZING)

01:34.866 --> 01:36.171
Wow.

01:49.552 --> 01:50.618
Hi, Millie!

01:50.654 --> 01:53.016
Hi, Mrs. Winchester!

01:53.052 --> 01:54.083
So nice to meet you.

01:54.119 --> 01:55.353
Please call me Nina.

01:55.389 --> 01:57.288
I've got some tea for us
and a charcuterie board.

01:57.323 --> 01:58.721
Is it too early
for meat and cheese?

01:58.756 --> 02:02.164
You know, that's what they have
for breakfast in Europe.

02:03.263 --> 02:06.300
MILLIE: Wow, um,
you're just, this is...

02:07.097 --> 02:09.098
I... I...

02:09.133 --> 02:12.469
I'm just going to say,
I think you might be
overqualified for this job

02:12.505 --> 02:14.740
with all this experience
and a college degree.

02:14.775 --> 02:15.802
No, I know.

02:15.838 --> 02:18.644
I just realized I really
enjoy being a housemaid.

02:18.679 --> 02:19.540
You do?

02:19.576 --> 02:21.711
For the right families,
of course.

02:22.613 --> 02:25.949
Okay. What brought you back
to New York?

02:25.984 --> 02:27.487
I missed it.

02:27.523 --> 02:30.653
Well, I really love New England,
but I miss being in the city.

02:30.688 --> 02:34.358
But you know this is
a live-in position, right?

02:34.394 --> 02:36.295
I mentioned that in the ad,
didn't I?

02:36.330 --> 02:37.928
Oh, yes. Oh, yeah.
No, of course. Yes. Yes.

02:37.964 --> 02:39.397
Oh, God, okay.

02:39.432 --> 02:41.197
-(EXCLAIMS)
-I miss being near the city,

02:41.233 --> 02:42.967
not actually in the city.

02:43.003 --> 02:44.432
It's a little crazy.

02:44.467 --> 02:47.670
Yes, I fully agree with you.

02:47.706 --> 02:50.704
Okay, so the job is
mostly organizing, cleaning,

02:50.739 --> 02:52.407
light cooking,
if you're up for that.

02:52.443 --> 02:53.943
Oh, absolutely.
I love to cook.

02:53.978 --> 02:55.316
Amazing.

02:55.351 --> 02:56.849
And then you would be
helping me with my daughter.

02:56.885 --> 02:59.220
She's Cecilia, Cece.

02:59.256 --> 03:02.187
She's seven years old
and, well, she's amazing.

03:02.222 --> 03:03.819
Well, I can't wait
to meet her.

03:04.254 --> 03:06.421
Oh. Good. Okay.

03:06.456 --> 03:08.288
Would you like a grand tour

03:08.324 --> 03:10.163
so you can...

03:10.198 --> 03:12.093
see what you're
getting yourself into?

03:12.128 --> 03:13.328
Sure.

03:13.363 --> 03:16.030
NINA: And the kitchen.

03:16.065 --> 03:20.169
My husband, Andrew, designed
this entire house soup to nuts.

03:20.204 --> 03:21.335
He's an architect?

03:21.370 --> 03:22.636
No, he's in tech.

03:22.672 --> 03:25.272
But he pays
incredible attention

03:25.308 --> 03:26.610
to every detail.

03:26.646 --> 03:30.143
Now, these steps are, uh,
kind of nuts, I know.

03:30.179 --> 03:32.914
Andrew says I'm totally gonna
kill myself one day on these.

03:33.448 --> 03:34.948
I'm such a klutz.

03:34.984 --> 03:37.418
I should just draw
my chalk outline on the bottom

03:37.453 --> 03:38.586
and get it over with.

03:38.622 --> 03:39.894
So there's another set
of stairs

03:39.929 --> 03:40.961
on the other side of the house

03:40.996 --> 03:42.730
that are less Guggenheim-y.

03:42.766 --> 03:44.024
If you're into that.

03:48.230 --> 03:49.367
Wow.

03:49.403 --> 03:51.406
NINA: It's basically
Andrew's man cave,

03:51.441 --> 03:55.041
but you are welcome to use it
anytime you want, of course.

03:55.076 --> 03:56.309
You'd be part of the family,

03:56.345 --> 03:58.340
which also means
that you would definitely have

03:58.376 --> 03:59.810
to listen to his TED Talk

03:59.845 --> 04:04.011
about how Barry Lyndon is
a misunderstood masterpiece.

04:06.285 --> 04:08.321
This is the upper living room,

04:08.356 --> 04:10.817
which we barely ever use,
to be honest.

04:10.852 --> 04:13.357
You sure you even need
a housekeeper?

04:13.393 --> 04:16.164
Well, actually,
I'm... expecting.

04:16.199 --> 04:18.229
So I'm not gonna have
quite so much time

04:18.264 --> 04:20.201
to keep everything so perfect.

04:20.237 --> 04:22.964
But don't tell Andrew
because it's very early

04:22.999 --> 04:26.234
and I want to be sure,
you know, before I tell him.

04:26.270 --> 04:27.839
Yeah. Congrats.

04:27.875 --> 04:28.937
Thank you.

04:30.044 --> 04:31.879
This is Cece's room.

04:31.915 --> 04:32.873
Andrew even made a little

04:32.908 --> 04:35.444
miniature version
of our house for her.

04:35.479 --> 04:36.945
-Isn't that sweet?
-Wow.

04:43.226 --> 04:45.356
NINA: So the laundry room is
in the basement,

04:45.392 --> 04:48.126
and that would be
your bathroom

04:48.162 --> 04:50.365
and you would be upstairs.

04:51.861 --> 04:53.935
You're gonna think
it's a little bit small,

04:53.970 --> 04:55.898
but it's got a lot of privacy,

04:55.934 --> 04:58.169
and we figured that that was
the most important thing.

04:58.204 --> 05:00.267
Lots of light, though.

05:00.302 --> 05:01.505
Ta-da!

05:01.540 --> 05:03.410
You can make it your own,
of course.

05:03.446 --> 05:05.807
You can hang posters
and bring in potted plants.

05:05.842 --> 05:07.709
You can blast your music
as loud as you want

05:07.745 --> 05:10.477
because we cannot
hear you downstairs.

05:10.512 --> 05:11.782
What do you think?

05:13.352 --> 05:14.983
-It's perfect.
-Okay, good.

05:16.186 --> 05:17.486
Win!

05:17.521 --> 05:19.160
Well, I'm still interviewing,

05:19.195 --> 05:21.627
but I'm hoping
to make a decision soon.

05:22.699 --> 05:24.098
Here you go.

05:24.134 --> 05:25.162
Oh, no, you don't
have to do that.

05:25.197 --> 05:26.299
Oh, no, I insist.

05:26.334 --> 05:27.465
You spent your energy
and your time

05:27.501 --> 05:29.096
and your gas money
to be here. Please.

05:30.169 --> 05:31.571
I appreciate it.

05:31.607 --> 05:35.005
I have a really good feeling
about this, Millie. I do.

05:35.040 --> 05:36.570
Me too.

05:36.605 --> 05:38.174
Okay. I'll be in touch.

05:38.209 --> 05:39.475
(INAUDIBLE)

05:39.511 --> 05:40.844
MILLIE: She won't be in touch.

05:40.879 --> 05:44.050
That's the last time I'll ever
set foot in that house.

05:44.085 --> 05:45.520
 One background check,

05:45.555 --> 05:48.616
and she'll see that everything
on that resume is a total lie.

05:48.651 --> 05:50.456
 I don't even wear glasses.

05:50.491 --> 05:52.419
 I'm just...
 I'm trying to look legit.

05:52.454 --> 05:53.725
 So stupid.

06:00.464 --> 06:02.030
(HAND DRYER BLOWING)

06:08.274 --> 06:09.972
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

06:12.677 --> 06:14.276
Um, can I get
a job application?

06:14.311 --> 06:15.983
Yeah, sure.

06:16.018 --> 06:17.716
-There you go.
-Thanks.

06:26.325 --> 06:27.561
(HAND DRYER BLOWING)

06:28.396 --> 06:30.025
MILLIE: I knew
 she wouldn't call.

06:30.060 --> 06:31.959
 Why did I even think I had
 a shot at that job?

06:31.994 --> 06:34.997
 Oh, well, at least I got
 $20 out of it.

06:36.603 --> 06:38.770
(SIGHS) I don't know
 what I'm gonna do.

06:48.951 --> 06:49.979
Roll it down.

06:52.416 --> 06:53.921
Can't sleep here.

06:53.956 --> 06:55.652
I'm so sorry. I...

06:55.687 --> 06:57.255
I was driving
from my mom's house

06:57.290 --> 06:58.591
and I got really sleepy,

06:58.627 --> 07:00.356
and I just I pulled over
to take a nap. I'm sorry.

07:00.391 --> 07:02.826
(PHONE VIBRATING)

07:02.862 --> 07:04.560
This is her actually.
Do you mind if I take it?

07:04.595 --> 07:05.934
She's probably freaking out.

07:05.969 --> 07:07.429
Don't text and drive.

07:07.465 --> 07:08.899
I won't. I promise.

07:12.067 --> 07:14.569
-Hello?
 -Hi, may I speak to Millie?

07:14.604 --> 07:17.242
Uh, this is her. She.

07:17.278 --> 07:19.005
 This is Nina Winchester.

07:19.041 --> 07:21.007
 I'm calling
 to offer you the job.

07:21.042 --> 07:23.649
 I mean, if you're
 still available.

07:23.685 --> 07:25.616
 Uh, you've probably got
 a million job offers.

07:25.651 --> 07:27.684
No. I mean, yes, yes.
I would love to.

07:27.719 --> 07:29.886
Uh, when would
you like me to start?

07:29.922 --> 07:33.622
 Oh, my goodness. (SIGHS)
 As soon as possible?

07:33.658 --> 07:35.093
Well, what about
this afternoon?

07:35.129 --> 07:36.329
 You know what?

07:36.365 --> 07:37.925
 -That would be great.
-Great.

07:37.960 --> 07:39.765
 Anyway, gotta run.
 Bye, Millie.

07:40.300 --> 07:41.668
MILLIE: (SOFTLY) Yes!

07:50.541 --> 07:53.141
-(CLICK)
-(LINE RINGING)

07:55.719 --> 07:56.782
Hey!

07:58.288 --> 07:59.385
-Hey, I'm Millie.
-(LINE RINGING)

07:59.421 --> 08:01.918
Do you work
for the Winchesters?

08:01.954 --> 08:04.452
I'm trying to get in,
but I don't know the code.

08:04.487 --> 08:05.519
(LINE BEEPS)

08:05.555 --> 08:06.792
(GATES CLANK)

08:30.787 --> 08:31.817
Nina?

08:33.682 --> 08:35.117
Nina, it's Millie.

08:41.061 --> 08:42.091
Nina?

08:51.132 --> 08:53.234
NINA: Millie?
Millie, Millie, Millie!

08:54.077 --> 08:55.443
(EXCLAIMS) Welcome. Hi.

08:55.478 --> 08:57.371
Sorry. I, um, meant
to leave the gate open.

08:57.406 --> 09:00.311
Do you need me to help you bring
in your stuff from your car?

09:00.347 --> 09:01.643
Oh, no, this is it.

09:01.678 --> 09:03.815
-Great. Wow.
-Yeah.

09:03.851 --> 09:05.478
Yeah, no, I put the rest of it
in a storage unit.

09:05.514 --> 09:07.916
Okay, well, that's great. I'm
gonna put these up in your room.

09:07.951 --> 09:10.818
Listen, I need
to write a PTA speech

09:10.853 --> 09:12.921
that has to be a barn burner,

09:12.956 --> 09:14.388
so I'm gonna be
stuck in my office.

09:14.423 --> 09:16.631
But the cleaning supplies are
in this closet over there,

09:17.066 --> 09:19.300
and... um, oh.

09:19.336 --> 09:21.295
You're not wearing
your glasses.

09:21.330 --> 09:24.364
Oh, I don't... I don't wear 'em
all the time. Contacts.

09:26.040 --> 09:27.133
Oh.

09:27.168 --> 09:29.006
Yeah, you look better
without them.

09:29.946 --> 09:31.107
Yeah. Okay.

09:31.608 --> 09:33.709
I'll be upstairs.

09:33.744 --> 09:35.208
This is gonna be fun, Millie!

09:35.243 --> 09:37.245
(TUMBLING DICE BY
LINDA RONSTADT PLAYING)

09:41.285 --> 09:45.659
♪ People try to rape me
 Always think I'm crazy ♪

09:45.695 --> 09:49.323
♪ Make me burn
 the candle right down ♪

09:50.561 --> 09:52.466
♪ Baby ♪

09:52.501 --> 09:54.564
(SONG CONTINUES PLAYING
ON HEADPHONES)

09:54.600 --> 09:56.330
No shoes on the furniture.

10:00.042 --> 10:02.637
Um, hey. Hi.

10:02.673 --> 10:05.405
You must be... Cece.

10:06.081 --> 10:07.308
I'm Millie.

10:08.115 --> 10:09.145
Hello.

10:09.879 --> 10:12.216
Oh, hey. Hi! You met Millie.

10:12.252 --> 10:13.079
Hi, baby.

10:13.115 --> 10:15.189
Millie's gonna be
living with us,

10:15.225 --> 10:16.049
and she's gonna be helping

10:16.085 --> 10:17.388
with the cooking
and the cleaning.

10:17.423 --> 10:18.625
And you know what?

10:18.660 --> 10:20.153
She might even play
 Candy Land with you

10:20.188 --> 10:22.427
if you ask her
with a pretty please.

10:22.463 --> 10:23.926
She's gonna live with us?

10:23.961 --> 10:26.361
(LAUGHING) Yes.
Andrew, I told you that.

10:26.397 --> 10:30.571
I said she was gonna be living
in the guest room in the attic.

10:30.607 --> 10:33.070
Doesn't this place look
incredible. Look at it.

10:35.709 --> 10:38.309
-Thank you.
-Well, Millie, welcome.

10:38.345 --> 10:39.709
Uh, thank you.

10:39.745 --> 10:41.044
Are you hungry?
I'm sure we can

10:41.080 --> 10:42.648
turn this dinner for three
into a dinner for four.

10:42.683 --> 10:44.747
No, I'm probably
just gonna go upstairs

10:44.782 --> 10:47.080
and, uh, get all settled in.

10:47.115 --> 10:48.314
-You sure?
-If you don't mind,

10:48.349 --> 10:50.888
I'll just come down afterwards
and tidy up.

10:50.923 --> 10:53.053
Yeah, get settled.
Yeah, take your time.

10:53.089 --> 10:54.562
We're so happy
that you're here.

10:54.597 --> 10:56.192
You just let us know
if you change your mind.

10:57.131 --> 10:58.194
Thanks.

11:03.398 --> 11:05.465
You ordered from the wrong
Italian place again.

11:41.673 --> 11:42.909
NINA: Knock, knock.

11:44.277 --> 11:45.104
Hi.

11:45.139 --> 11:47.308
That window doesn't open, sadly.

11:47.343 --> 11:49.210
But there's a lot
of ventilation in this room,

11:49.245 --> 11:51.252
so you should never
get stuffy in here.

11:51.287 --> 11:52.616
I got you some dinner.

11:52.652 --> 11:55.320
Andrew always over-orders.

11:55.356 --> 11:56.282
I put some water

11:56.318 --> 11:57.657
in the mini fridge,
did you see that?

11:57.693 --> 11:59.288
Yeah, I really don't
want to be a pain,

11:59.323 --> 12:02.058
but if it is possible to try
and get the window open,

12:02.093 --> 12:04.224
it'd be nice to get
some fresh air in here.

12:04.259 --> 12:06.766
Yeah, I agree.
That's a great idea.

12:06.801 --> 12:08.528
I will talk to the handyman
about that.

12:08.563 --> 12:11.231
Okay, cool. Is that the guy
that's down in the yard?

12:11.266 --> 12:13.437
No, that's Enzo.
He's the groundskeeper.

12:13.473 --> 12:14.809
Never mind him.

12:14.844 --> 12:16.839
And then if I could just
get a key for the deadbolt.

12:16.874 --> 12:19.809
Oh, my God, yes. The deadbolt.

12:19.844 --> 12:22.642
(CHUCKLES) That's so creepy.

12:22.677 --> 12:26.483
This used to be Andrew's storage
closet for his files. Okay?

12:26.519 --> 12:27.954
But, oh, my God,

12:28.456 --> 12:30.352
closed window, deadbolt.

12:31.988 --> 12:33.658
What kind of monsters are we?

12:33.694 --> 12:35.527
-Uh...
-I will sort that out.

12:35.563 --> 12:37.227
Oh, before I forget. Um...

12:38.830 --> 12:40.462
This is for you. A present.

12:40.497 --> 12:43.569
Also, just, I saw that your
phone was just really ancient,

12:43.604 --> 12:45.838
and I wanted you to have that

12:45.873 --> 12:48.708
because I uploaded
the credit card onto it

12:48.744 --> 12:49.770
so you can use it
at the grocery store

12:49.805 --> 12:51.075
and for gas.

12:51.110 --> 12:53.508
Oh, um, I'll take good care
of it. Thank you.

12:53.543 --> 12:58.919
Honestly, I'm like, so happy
that... you're here with us.

12:59.583 --> 13:00.948
Thanks.

13:00.983 --> 13:02.516
Can I give you a hug?

13:04.493 --> 13:06.358
(SIGHS) Thank you, Millie.

13:06.394 --> 13:08.354
Thank you. Okay.

13:08.390 --> 13:10.227
Let me know
if you need anything else.

13:27.842 --> 13:29.246
(YAWNS)

13:35.553 --> 13:36.583
Shit.

13:44.826 --> 13:46.065
(CLICKS)

13:46.566 --> 13:49.269
(LOCK RATTLES)

13:49.304 --> 13:50.131
No, no, no.

13:50.167 --> 13:52.569
-(STRAINING)
-(DOORKNOB RATTLING)

13:52.604 --> 13:53.974
No, no, no.

13:54.475 --> 13:55.976
(DOOR CREAKS)

13:58.874 --> 14:00.112
(SHRIEKING)

14:07.585 --> 14:09.086
Nina?

14:09.121 --> 14:11.054
-(SHOUTING) Where are they?
-Where are what?

14:11.089 --> 14:13.254
My PTA notes
for the meeting tonight!

14:13.289 --> 14:14.725
They were right here
on the counter,

14:14.761 --> 14:15.861
and now they're not here.

14:15.896 --> 14:17.296
-Where are they?
-I didn't see any notes.

14:17.332 --> 14:18.562
Bullshit!

14:18.598 --> 14:19.626
Where are they?

14:20.867 --> 14:22.634
-Nina, no, no.
-ANDREW: Hey.

14:22.669 --> 14:23.970
Hey! What's going on?

14:24.006 --> 14:27.667
Millie threw away my notes
for the meeting tonight.

14:29.204 --> 14:31.110
(SHOUTING) Where are they?

14:32.914 --> 14:34.845
Nina, why don't we go
check your office?

14:34.881 --> 14:36.747
I have to get up
and do a speech

14:36.782 --> 14:37.979
in front of everybody

14:38.014 --> 14:39.313
and now I have nothing!

14:39.348 --> 14:41.786
-(OBJECTS CLATTERING)
-(SHRIEKING)

14:41.822 --> 14:43.590
-ANDREW: Nina!
-(YELLING) What?

14:43.626 --> 14:45.859
-(DRAWER SLIDING SHUT)
-(THUDS)

14:45.894 --> 14:48.094
-Do you have a copy...
-(VESSELS CLINKING)

14:48.662 --> 14:49.892
...on your computer?

14:49.927 --> 14:52.032
I wrote them by hand!

14:52.565 --> 14:54.197
Oh, fuck!

14:54.233 --> 14:56.535
I always think better
when I write by hand.

14:56.571 --> 14:58.104
Where's my nail at?

14:58.705 --> 15:00.271
(SHRIEKS AND WHIMPERS)

15:00.836 --> 15:05.175
(CRYING)

15:05.210 --> 15:06.810
ANDREW: All right.
Come here, come here.

15:06.846 --> 15:08.983
-(CRYING)
-It's okay.

15:10.450 --> 15:13.820
(CRYING)

15:13.856 --> 15:16.089
ANDREW: Let's take
a deep breath, okay?

15:16.124 --> 15:18.353
-(NINA CONTINUES CRYING)
-Breathe, breathe, breathe.

15:18.388 --> 15:20.824
-Breathe, breathe, breathe.
-(SNIFFLES)

15:20.859 --> 15:23.063
(EXHALES AND SNIFFLES)

15:23.664 --> 15:24.966
I'm gonna pick you up.

15:28.034 --> 15:29.336
-(NINA CRIES)
-(ANDREW GRUNTS SOFTLY)

15:29.372 --> 15:31.599
(NINA SOBBING)

15:35.671 --> 15:38.674
Here's the plan. I am going
to take Cece to school,

15:38.710 --> 15:40.407
and you...

15:40.442 --> 15:42.850
you are going to take
a hot shower.

15:42.885 --> 15:44.380
You're gonna have
a nice long breakfast,

15:44.416 --> 15:46.317
and then you have all day
to work on your speech,

15:46.353 --> 15:49.617
and you can still make it
to the salon for a touch up.

15:49.652 --> 15:51.590
You'll have just enough time
to get your roots done.

15:51.626 --> 15:52.824
I love you so much.

15:52.859 --> 15:54.226
-I love you.
-I love you.

15:57.294 --> 15:59.561
You need to be
more careful next time.

16:01.670 --> 16:03.334
You've ruined my entire day.

16:05.000 --> 16:06.238
I'm sorry.

16:11.447 --> 16:12.673
(ANDREW SIGHS)

16:15.077 --> 16:16.314
I am so sorry.

16:17.620 --> 16:18.711
Don-- Don't worry about it.

16:18.747 --> 16:20.452
I don't know what's been
going on with her lately.

16:20.487 --> 16:22.088
She's...

16:22.123 --> 16:24.757
she's been on a real
emotional roller coaster.

16:24.792 --> 16:26.522
Oh, it's probably the hor--

16:27.927 --> 16:30.127
um, Mercury in retrograde.

16:30.162 --> 16:31.991
Didn't peg you
for the star-chart type.

16:32.026 --> 16:33.430
Guilty.

16:36.672 --> 16:38.237
Let me help you clean up.

16:38.272 --> 16:39.805
-It's a fuckin' mess in here.
-No, no, no. I got it.

16:39.840 --> 16:41.941
I got it. You go get ready.

16:41.976 --> 16:43.473
I don't want you
to be late for Cece.

16:44.578 --> 16:45.673
Thank you.

16:48.611 --> 16:51.250
-(TAPS COUNTERTOP)
-Tomorrow will be better.

16:53.249 --> 16:55.221
It'll be better, I promise.

16:55.786 --> 16:56.816
Okay.

17:02.324 --> 17:03.894
-Yeah.
-(TAPS COUNTERTOP)

17:03.930 --> 17:06.298
Cece! Let's hit the road!

17:07.768 --> 17:09.565
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYS)

17:26.550 --> 17:28.155
(IN NON-NATIVE ACCENT)
What are you doing here?

17:28.754 --> 17:30.124
I work here.

17:31.055 --> 17:32.720
What are you doing here?

17:33.626 --> 17:35.162
You...

17:43.166 --> 17:47.141
(MUTTERS IN ITALIAN)

18:03.285 --> 18:04.752
-(YAWNS)
-(BUCKET THUDS)

18:09.929 --> 18:12.727
(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

18:25.375 --> 18:27.109
I don't really
fit in very well

18:27.145 --> 18:29.183
with those other PTA moms.

18:30.416 --> 18:33.078
I guess I didn't realize
how stressed I've been.

18:33.114 --> 18:36.718
It's probably just all the new
hormones making you go crazy.

18:39.357 --> 18:41.054
I wouldn't say anything
to Andrew.

18:41.089 --> 18:42.427
Get out.

18:42.961 --> 18:44.096
I have to shower.

18:44.131 --> 18:45.961
And you're gonna
handle dinner later.

18:45.997 --> 18:47.234
MILLIE: Yeah.

18:48.001 --> 18:49.132
ANDREW: It smells amazing.

18:49.167 --> 18:50.966
MILLIE: It's chicken piccata.

18:51.001 --> 18:52.234
ANDREW: Mmm.

18:52.269 --> 18:54.470
Oh, I picked this up for Cece.

18:54.506 --> 18:57.439
Oh, these are fantastic.
She's gonna love these.

18:57.474 --> 18:58.672
Someone did not
get her snack today,

18:58.707 --> 19:01.077
and she's a very hungry
little ballerina.

19:01.112 --> 19:02.580
(MILLIE CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

19:02.615 --> 19:05.045
Why don't you get her started,
and I'll be right back down?

19:05.080 --> 19:06.484
Okay.

19:08.985 --> 19:10.290
(SIGHS)

19:12.220 --> 19:13.656
Hey, Cece,

19:14.025 --> 19:15.361
how was class?

19:16.896 --> 19:18.065
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

19:18.100 --> 19:21.494
Would you, uh, like juice
or... or water?

19:21.530 --> 19:24.271
Juice.
But this glass is dirty.

19:25.207 --> 19:26.971
Really? I just took it out
of the dishwasher.

19:27.006 --> 19:28.273
Juice is a privilege.

19:28.309 --> 19:30.739
Not something you drink
out of a dirty glass.

19:32.175 --> 19:33.445
Of course not.

19:34.747 --> 19:35.777
(SIGHS)

19:46.894 --> 19:48.625
This looks amazing.

19:48.660 --> 19:51.562
Doesn't it, Cece? Way better
than dinosaur nuggets.

19:53.261 --> 19:54.795
Hey, Millie,

19:54.830 --> 19:57.700
why don't you grab
a place setting and join us?

19:58.705 --> 19:59.740
Uh...

19:59.775 --> 20:01.201
No, I... I already ate.

20:01.237 --> 20:02.507
Oh, we insist.

20:03.338 --> 20:04.806
Don't we, Cece?

20:07.076 --> 20:08.315
Um...

20:09.345 --> 20:10.977
I hope you guys like it.

20:30.970 --> 20:32.570
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

20:33.740 --> 20:34.869
Come in.

20:37.238 --> 20:39.242
Hey.

20:39.278 --> 20:41.447
-Hey.
-Sorry to bother you.

20:42.950 --> 20:44.277
Got something for you.

20:44.313 --> 20:45.682
Cece insisted.

20:46.547 --> 20:48.586
-She's so sweet.
-Yeah.

20:50.787 --> 20:53.723
(WHY IS SHE STILL HERE?
BY RENEE RAPP PLAYING)

20:57.625 --> 20:59.999
♪ You can tell me ♪

21:00.034 --> 21:01.829
♪ You don't love her ♪

21:01.865 --> 21:05.137
♪ But you should
 probably tell her too ♪

21:05.172 --> 21:06.265
♪ 'Cause I can't keep... ♪

21:06.300 --> 21:07.572
(GASPS)

21:08.072 --> 21:09.304
No, no, no.

21:09.339 --> 21:11.675
Absolutely fucking not!

21:12.714 --> 21:13.743
Oh, my God.

21:22.452 --> 21:24.655
I want you to feel safe here.

21:26.727 --> 21:27.757
I do.

21:30.526 --> 21:32.432
For your door, as requested.

21:32.964 --> 21:34.500
Thanks.

21:38.107 --> 21:40.440
So how was last night?
With Andrew?

21:41.874 --> 21:43.338
Good.

21:43.373 --> 21:45.005
I made chicken piccata.

21:46.211 --> 21:48.008
He's a dream, isn't he?

21:49.515 --> 21:51.312
He pretends to like everything
I make him,

21:51.348 --> 21:52.584
even if he hates it.

21:58.121 --> 21:59.393
Mmm.

22:02.096 --> 22:04.062
That's a lot of bacon, Millie.

22:04.098 --> 22:05.795
Are you trying to kill us?

22:11.401 --> 22:12.769
Where are you going?

22:15.040 --> 22:16.237
I have...

22:16.273 --> 22:17.572
Saturday off.

22:17.608 --> 22:18.704
Isn't that
what we talked about?

22:18.740 --> 22:21.745
No, I...
I can't spare you today.

22:22.613 --> 22:24.647
I missed
my hair salon appointment

22:24.682 --> 22:28.116
because you threw away
my notes. (CHUCKLES)

22:28.152 --> 22:29.749
Remember?

22:29.785 --> 22:32.857
I have a meeting
that I can't miss.

22:32.892 --> 22:34.157
(SCOFFS)

22:34.193 --> 22:35.561
You have a meeting?

22:36.129 --> 22:37.563
What's the meeting for?

22:40.401 --> 22:42.034
If I could just have
a couple hours off,

22:42.069 --> 22:43.101
and then I'll come back.

22:43.136 --> 22:45.437
Millie, absolutely not.

22:45.472 --> 22:47.273
-ANDREW: Baby?
-I can't have you... What?

22:47.308 --> 22:49.542
Sweetheart, it's okay.
She can go.

22:51.040 --> 22:53.140
-But, Andy, it's your day off.
-I know, exactly.

22:53.176 --> 22:56.613
And that's why we're gonna go
to the park... fly this kite.

22:56.649 --> 22:57.778
And we've been waiting
all week to fly, right?

22:57.814 --> 22:58.744
We're doing donuts,
we're doing kites,

22:58.779 --> 23:00.487
and then we're doing ballet.

23:02.056 --> 23:03.083
Go. Take your time.

23:07.062 --> 23:09.188
-Bye, Mama.
-Bye, baby.

23:11.427 --> 23:14.701
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

23:14.737 --> 23:15.865
Have fun.

23:20.368 --> 23:21.640
Thanks.

23:23.977 --> 23:25.072
(DOOR OPENS)

23:27.049 --> 23:28.475
PAM: Hey, how are you doin'?

23:28.510 --> 23:30.248
MILLIE: I'm good.

23:30.283 --> 23:31.679
Still writing in your journal?

23:31.715 --> 23:34.655
Uh, yeah.
Do you wanna read it?

23:34.690 --> 23:35.585
God, no.

23:35.620 --> 23:38.357
I have enough shit
to read as it is.

23:38.392 --> 23:40.660
So you left the job
at Charlie's?

23:40.695 --> 23:44.497
Well, this housekeeping job
just sort of fell into my lap.

23:44.533 --> 23:47.065
And it's live-in,
so I'm saving a fortune on rent.

23:47.100 --> 23:49.135
Okay, that's good.

23:49.170 --> 23:52.037
I have my new address here,

23:52.072 --> 23:53.601
and phone number.

23:53.636 --> 23:56.075
The family is really amazing.

23:56.110 --> 23:57.577
I feel... I feel lucky.

23:57.612 --> 23:59.805
Must make meeting new people
a little tough, though,

23:59.840 --> 24:01.413
having to live with a family.

24:01.448 --> 24:02.813
I mean, you would
think that, right?

24:02.848 --> 24:06.813
But I have already met
a ton of really cool nannies.

24:06.849 --> 24:08.654
Any mannies in there?
(CHUCKLES)

24:09.556 --> 24:12.422
Are you asking me
about my love life, Pam?

24:12.457 --> 24:13.789
If I know how Tinder works,

24:13.824 --> 24:16.660
or if I'm horn dogging
all over Great Neck

24:16.696 --> 24:18.026
because I haven't gotten laid
in ten years?

24:18.061 --> 24:20.930
No. I'm just saying
human connections are important.

24:22.299 --> 24:23.565
Definitely.

24:23.601 --> 24:25.704
But hold onto this job,
Millie.

24:26.405 --> 24:27.805
And the living situation.

24:29.742 --> 24:31.939
You'll need both,
or you'll be back at Bedford

24:31.975 --> 24:35.379
serving the five years
left on your sentence.

24:35.414 --> 24:37.613
And I don't like that for you.

24:37.649 --> 24:39.817
I don't like that
for me, either.

24:42.650 --> 24:45.251
(PHONE VIBRATING)

24:48.663 --> 24:50.463
-Hi, Nina, I'm just--
 -I need you to pick up Cece

24:50.499 --> 24:53.395
 from ballet class, 1:45,
 and don't be late.

24:53.430 --> 24:54.629
(LINE DISCONNECTS)

24:54.664 --> 24:57.670
Um, okay, where is it? Nina?

24:59.302 --> 25:00.640
What?

25:02.010 --> 25:03.236
Ballet school?

25:03.671 --> 25:04.908
Ballet class.

25:06.915 --> 25:08.342
Little kids.

25:08.377 --> 25:10.116
Fuck.

25:10.151 --> 25:11.515
INSTRUCTOR: Tendu right.

25:11.551 --> 25:15.020
And curtsy
and open to the left.

25:15.056 --> 25:16.354
Foot behind you.

25:16.389 --> 25:18.885
Excellent, and close to first.

25:18.921 --> 25:20.788
Fabulous class today.
Thank you.

25:20.824 --> 25:22.955
Let's go get
our bags and shoes.

25:22.991 --> 25:25.632
-Great job.
-(DOORBELL CHIMING)

25:26.699 --> 25:29.695
-Hi. Who are you looking for?
-Uh, Cece.

25:29.731 --> 25:31.566
Cecilia Winchester.

25:31.601 --> 25:32.969
Are you Nina's new girl?

25:33.736 --> 25:36.302
-Yes. Hi, I'm Millie.
-Hi.

25:37.638 --> 25:38.905
MILLIE: Hi!

25:38.941 --> 25:41.677
Cece! Hey,
I'm here to pick you up.

25:41.713 --> 25:43.814
I'm spending the night
at Emma's.

25:43.850 --> 25:46.579
We arranged it weeks ago.
She has all her things.

25:46.615 --> 25:47.917
Oh, no, no, no.

25:47.953 --> 25:49.553
Nina just called me
and asked me to pick her up,

25:49.589 --> 25:50.990
so she probably
changed her mind.

25:51.025 --> 25:52.588
PATRICE: Oh.

25:52.623 --> 25:54.287
(EXHALES) Okay, let me check.

25:58.592 --> 25:59.864
Nina!

26:00.332 --> 26:02.566
Hi, it's Patrice.

26:02.602 --> 26:04.467
Your girl is here.
She's insisting

26:04.503 --> 26:07.003
she needs to pick up Cece.

26:09.275 --> 26:10.875
(PATRICE CHUCKLES)

26:12.210 --> 26:13.306
I know.

26:13.981 --> 26:14.940
I know.

26:14.975 --> 26:16.944
No, it's no problem at all.

26:16.979 --> 26:19.620
It's impossible to find
reliable help.

26:20.321 --> 26:22.450
Oh, would you like to confirm?

26:22.486 --> 26:23.954
(MILLIE INHALES)

26:24.927 --> 26:26.055
Have fun.

26:28.228 --> 26:29.558
We figured it out.

26:29.593 --> 26:32.193
Okay, take care. Bye.

26:32.961 --> 26:34.930
Wow,
they really are beautiful.

26:34.965 --> 26:37.103
NINA: So happy
we'll be able to use them,

26:37.138 --> 26:38.197
Mother Winchester.

26:38.232 --> 26:41.037
Well, the pattern is vintage,
of course.

26:41.670 --> 26:42.940
NINA: Millie.

26:45.174 --> 26:47.644
I told you Cece was having
a sleepover tonight.

26:47.680 --> 26:49.910
There was no need
to make a scene.

26:49.946 --> 26:51.443
-(MILLIE INHALES)
-(MOTHER SIGHS)

26:51.478 --> 26:55.588
This is how you allow the help
to dress in your home?

26:55.623 --> 26:57.618
Uh, this is Andrew's mother,
Mrs. Winchester.

26:57.653 --> 26:58.855
She's downsizing,

26:58.890 --> 27:01.019
so she has brought us
her mother's china.

27:01.055 --> 27:02.795
-Yes.
-NINA: Isn't it lovely?

27:04.131 --> 27:05.699
Isn't it?

27:06.431 --> 27:08.399
-Yes.
-I know.

27:08.435 --> 27:11.034
Andrew loves these dishes.

27:11.601 --> 27:13.668
I want you...

27:13.704 --> 27:15.201
to put them somewhere safe

27:15.236 --> 27:17.937
'cause Nina's likely
to trip over herself

27:17.972 --> 27:19.709
and smash them all to pieces.

27:19.745 --> 27:20.909
-(MOTHER CHUCKLES)
-(DOOR OPENS)

27:20.944 --> 27:22.876
-Guilty as charged.
-(DOOR CLOSES)

27:22.911 --> 27:24.583
-MOTHER: Andrew!
-ANDREW: Oh.

27:24.618 --> 27:27.147
-Mother.
-Oh, Andrew, where's your tie?

27:27.182 --> 27:29.919
ANDREW: I know,
I'm too casual. I'm sorry.

27:29.954 --> 27:31.851
-Your hair is fabulous.
-Thank you, darling.

27:31.887 --> 27:34.022
Not a root in sight. Is...

27:34.057 --> 27:35.726
-Is that what I think it is?
-Yes, it is.

27:35.761 --> 27:37.725
Can't wait to eat off
of those plates.

27:37.761 --> 27:39.431
MOTHER: Family heirlooms.

27:39.466 --> 27:41.394
-So happy it's back.
-Me too.

27:45.204 --> 27:46.465
(SIGHS)

27:47.872 --> 27:50.106
This fucking window.
(GROANS SOFTLY)

27:54.743 --> 27:56.678
(GROANS SOFTLY)

27:56.713 --> 27:58.246
(WOOD SQUEAKING SOFTLY)

28:19.600 --> 28:21.137
(WOMAN SPEAKING ON TV)
 Dishes are still in the sink.

28:21.172 --> 28:23.169
MAN 1: Yeah, I know.
 I'm kinda lettin' em soak.

28:23.204 --> 28:24.609
WOMAN: Uh,
 they've been soaking

28:24.644 --> 28:26.305
 -for three days.
-(LAUGH TRACK)

28:26.340 --> 28:27.746
MAN: Well, now,
 you know, it's kinda...

28:27.781 --> 28:29.776
 Glug, glug, glug,
 glug, glug. Ding.

28:29.812 --> 28:31.518
 Glug, glug, glug.

28:31.553 --> 28:33.050
 ...home
 with everybody going out.

28:33.883 --> 28:34.947
 I'm going to ask you one...

28:34.982 --> 28:36.790
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

28:38.254 --> 28:40.022
MAN: I'm not gonna ask you
 what you sell.

28:40.058 --> 28:42.262
 I'm gonna go on here
 to Patsy, all right?

28:42.297 --> 28:43.797
ANDREW: Ah, Family Feud.

28:44.232 --> 28:45.894
I'm so sorry.

28:45.930 --> 28:47.699
Um... I...
I couldn't get some...

28:47.734 --> 28:48.965
-I'll leave you alone.
-No, no. Please.

28:49.001 --> 28:50.168
-Get out of your way.
-Sit, please. No, sit.

28:50.203 --> 28:51.464
Come on.

28:52.866 --> 28:54.538
Please stay.

28:54.573 --> 28:56.810
Oh, I love this show.

28:57.276 --> 28:58.975
Me too.

28:59.010 --> 29:01.614
I've only ever seen
the Steve Harvey one.

29:01.649 --> 29:03.712
-Really? Oh, this is classic.
-Yeah.

29:03.747 --> 29:05.217
This is Richard Dawson.

29:05.253 --> 29:06.787
Fashion icon.

29:07.355 --> 29:09.688
-He's an OG.
-Yeah?

29:09.723 --> 29:11.784
He has
some spectacular sideburns.

29:11.820 --> 29:13.485
He sure does.

29:13.520 --> 29:16.660
Man, my family would have
killed on this show.

29:16.695 --> 29:18.463
They are absolute vultures.

29:18.498 --> 29:19.532
Especially my mother.

29:19.568 --> 29:21.863
What about you?
You... your, um...

29:21.898 --> 29:23.364
parents, are they game people?

29:24.772 --> 29:27.369
Oh, we don't really
keep in touch anymore.

29:27.405 --> 29:28.437
Oh.

29:28.473 --> 29:29.502
I'm sorry.

29:30.444 --> 29:32.003
That's gotta be hard.

29:32.039 --> 29:34.407
Uh, not really, no.

29:34.443 --> 29:36.575
I mean, even if we were,
they probably wouldn't...

29:37.285 --> 29:38.882
be into this.

29:38.918 --> 29:41.354
They're kinda like
the opposite of fun.

29:41.390 --> 29:42.482
Well, I'll tell you what.

29:43.787 --> 29:45.254
You can be on our team.

29:46.625 --> 29:47.993
It'd be me and you...

29:49.023 --> 29:50.729
and Nina and my mom.

29:50.764 --> 29:52.558
Nina's parents don't
make the cut?

29:53.226 --> 29:55.132
They died when she was a kid.

29:55.898 --> 29:57.904
-That's awful.
-Yeah.

29:58.770 --> 30:00.373
It's a crazy story, actually.

30:00.409 --> 30:01.941
They died in a house fire.

30:02.875 --> 30:05.777
No one knows
how it was started.

30:05.813 --> 30:07.442
Nina made it out,
her parents didn't.

30:07.477 --> 30:10.180
For a long time, the police
actually thought that she...

30:14.718 --> 30:16.655
Can you imagine...

30:16.691 --> 30:19.055
living with that
your entire life?

30:19.090 --> 30:21.422
-That'd be terrible.
-What would be terrible?

30:22.958 --> 30:24.194
ANDREW: There she is.

30:24.627 --> 30:25.762
Hey.

30:25.797 --> 30:27.967
RICHARD: Name a cartoon bird.

30:28.567 --> 30:29.765
(BUZZER BEEPING)

30:29.800 --> 30:31.101
What are you doing up?

30:31.137 --> 30:33.065
What do you mean?
I can say the same about you.

30:33.101 --> 30:34.899
I'm watching Family Feud.

30:34.935 --> 30:36.105
NINA: Mmm.

30:36.140 --> 30:37.909
-At 2:00 a.m.?
-You wanna get in on this?

30:37.944 --> 30:40.479
Some Dawson? Wanna get
some Dawson on you?

30:40.514 --> 30:42.245
No, I'm good. It's...

30:42.978 --> 30:44.214
Baby, it's 2:00 a.m.

30:44.647 --> 30:45.919
Okay.

30:46.421 --> 30:47.882
I'mma go to bed. (SIGHS)

30:47.917 --> 30:49.450
Let me know how it ends.

30:51.292 --> 30:52.354
All right.

30:54.724 --> 30:55.962
Goodnight.

30:56.696 --> 30:58.525
-I'll be right up.
-Okay.

30:59.701 --> 31:02.028
 Uh, cartoon bird,
 little Katie.

31:02.064 --> 31:03.129
 Three answers remaining.

31:03.164 --> 31:04.770
-KATIE: Daffy Duck.
-Um.

31:04.806 --> 31:06.036
RICHARD: Let's see
 if you made it.

31:06.071 --> 31:09.409
It's late. I should
probably get some sleep.

31:09.444 --> 31:10.640
(PEOPLE CHEERING ON TV)

31:10.675 --> 31:11.707
(REMOTE CLICKING)

31:11.743 --> 31:13.144
This isn't working.

31:13.878 --> 31:16.213
-What?
-This isn't working.

31:17.247 --> 31:19.851
So I'm gonna need you
to pack your stuff

31:19.886 --> 31:21.113
and leave
first thing in the morning

31:21.148 --> 31:22.648
before Cece wakes up.

31:23.492 --> 31:24.520
So she doesn't get upset.

31:24.556 --> 31:26.355
No, Nina.

31:27.559 --> 31:28.620
I... I...

31:28.655 --> 31:30.390
I didn't think anyone was
gonna be down here.

31:30.425 --> 31:32.061
You told me I could use
the screening room.

31:32.096 --> 31:33.827
I'm gonna need
the phone back as well.

31:33.863 --> 31:35.668
Please, Nina.

31:35.704 --> 31:37.670
-(SCOFFING)
-I will do anything

31:37.706 --> 31:39.406
to make it up to you.
I promise.

31:39.441 --> 31:40.501
Can you just give me...

31:41.376 --> 31:42.404
one more chance?

31:44.345 --> 31:45.407
(NINA SIGHS)

31:45.906 --> 31:47.145
Um...

31:47.644 --> 31:48.707
Fine.

31:50.285 --> 31:51.314
One week.

31:51.780 --> 31:53.182
Okay?

31:53.217 --> 31:55.984
But you're gonna
have to dress appropriately

31:56.019 --> 31:57.518
around the house from now on.

31:58.625 --> 32:00.158
Yeah, of course. Sorry.

32:05.993 --> 32:07.561
Oh, Millie.

32:10.068 --> 32:12.236
Stay the fuck away
from my husband.

32:12.936 --> 32:14.469
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYS)

32:27.454 --> 32:29.185
(OVEN DINGS)

32:29.220 --> 32:31.051
-JILIANNE: Mmm.
-And so my nanny's going on

32:31.087 --> 32:33.253
and on about her dead dog,

32:33.289 --> 32:36.161
and I don't mean
to be a B-I-T-C-H,

32:36.197 --> 32:38.995
but since when did I become
a canine grief counselor?

32:39.031 --> 32:41.360
Meanwhile,
Emma is late for school.

32:41.395 --> 32:43.834
-WOMEN: Mmm.
-I'm missing yoga.

32:43.870 --> 32:45.135
You know what yoga means
to me.

32:45.170 --> 32:47.405
-It's everything.
-That's so unfortunate.

32:47.441 --> 32:48.538
Thank you.

32:48.574 --> 32:49.668
(INHALES)

32:49.704 --> 32:53.044
Well, we are going to be
looking for a nanny soon.

32:53.079 --> 32:55.110
(GASPS) Oh, my God, Nina!
You're pregnant.

32:55.145 --> 32:57.483
-Nina. (CHUCKLES)
-I knew it.

32:57.519 --> 32:59.585
No. Not... Not yet.

32:59.620 --> 33:01.414
We are making a plan.

33:01.449 --> 33:03.118
We've been going to see
this incredible

33:03.154 --> 33:04.755
fertility specialist
in the city.

33:04.790 --> 33:06.119
-Cool.
-Andrew insists

33:06.154 --> 33:07.724
on sparing no expense,

33:07.760 --> 33:09.324
of course. So, yeah.

33:09.359 --> 33:11.658
-That's wonderful.
-JILIANNE: Ooh, yeah.

33:11.694 --> 33:14.831
We will find you the most
fantastic nanny, I promise.

33:14.866 --> 33:16.197
-Absolutely.
-Thanks.

33:16.233 --> 33:18.497
Oh, this is
Cece's pediatrician.

33:18.532 --> 33:20.700
-I will be right back.
-SUZANNE: Oh.

33:21.707 --> 33:23.043
Fill our tea.

33:26.276 --> 33:27.373
JILIANNE: Oh, my God,
I'm so sorry.

33:27.409 --> 33:28.978
I really thought
she was pregnant.

33:29.014 --> 33:30.078
I know,
we were all thinking it.

33:30.114 --> 33:31.245
I mean,
have you seen her skin?

33:31.280 --> 33:32.818
God, and how about
those roots?

33:32.854 --> 33:33.985
My God.
You'd think she would take

33:34.020 --> 33:35.787
better care of herself
for Andrew.

33:35.823 --> 33:37.387
-He's so fucking hot.
-He is.

33:37.422 --> 33:39.989
And especially because
they have an airtight prenup.

33:40.025 --> 33:41.488
-JILIANNE: Mmm.
-Okay. You know,

33:41.524 --> 33:43.961
she did not have a dime
when they got married.

33:43.997 --> 33:45.293
She'll be sleeping
on the street

33:45.328 --> 33:46.658
if she doesn't get
her shit together.

33:46.693 --> 33:49.463
Cece? Would he get custody,
considering...

33:49.498 --> 33:52.567
PATRICE: Of course.
After what she did.

33:52.602 --> 33:54.866
How many months she spent
in that awful psych ward?

33:54.902 --> 33:56.906
-JILIANNE AND SUZANNE: Nine.
-(PATRICE CHUCKLING) Nine.

33:56.941 --> 33:58.137
Nine months. (SCOFFS)

33:58.172 --> 33:59.472
I mean, good Lord,

33:59.507 --> 34:00.911
I do not know
how he puts up with her.

34:00.947 --> 34:03.113
PATRICE:
Because he is a saint.

34:03.149 --> 34:04.544
-He's a hot saint.
-(PATRICE EXCLAIMS)

34:04.580 --> 34:08.084
-Hot Saint Andrew. Oh, my God.
-(ALL CHUCKLING)

34:08.120 --> 34:09.681
-SUZANNE: Ooh.
-What did I miss?

34:09.716 --> 34:12.757
Oh, we're just talking
spring fundraiser.

34:12.792 --> 34:13.824
-PATRICE: Ooh.
-Please,

34:13.860 --> 34:15.491
save us with a theme idea.

34:17.565 --> 34:19.593
Stop lurking.

34:19.628 --> 34:21.695
MILLIE: Those women were right
about one thing.

34:21.731 --> 34:24.565
 Andrew is definitely a saint
 for standing by Nina.

34:24.601 --> 34:27.005
 I can't believe she lied
 about being pregnant.

34:27.040 --> 34:29.206
 Everything she's told me
 is a lie.

34:29.242 --> 34:30.907
 It wasn't the hormones
 making her crazy.

34:30.942 --> 34:33.039
 She actually is crazy.

34:33.075 --> 34:34.276
 Poor Andrew.

34:34.312 --> 34:35.680
 As soon as I save up
 enough money,

34:35.716 --> 34:37.381
 I am out of here.

34:39.952 --> 34:42.122
Today wasn't a total disaster.

34:42.854 --> 34:44.618
Uh, thank you.

34:44.653 --> 34:46.653
I'm gonna need you
to watch Cece next Saturday.

34:46.688 --> 34:49.223
Andrew and I have
an appointment in the city,

34:49.258 --> 34:50.623
and I know it's your day off,

34:50.658 --> 34:53.333
but I trust
that it won't be a problem.

34:53.368 --> 34:54.431
Uh...

34:55.362 --> 34:57.566
-We'll have fun.
-Good.

35:25.962 --> 35:27.629
Haloperidol.

35:32.773 --> 35:34.867
Acute fucking psychosis?

35:38.441 --> 35:40.508
 Hey, Lexi,
 it's Millie. Listen.

35:40.543 --> 35:41.912
 I really need to make
 some extra money

35:41.947 --> 35:43.181
 so I can quit this job.

35:43.216 --> 35:45.413
Do you think
you could, um, ask your cousin

35:45.449 --> 35:48.018
if I could get a job
at the warehouse?

35:48.053 --> 35:49.186
I'll do anything. I'll clean,

35:49.221 --> 35:50.682
I'll set boxes,
I'll scrub toilets.

35:50.718 --> 35:52.987
I just really need
to get out of here.

35:53.023 --> 35:54.823
You're leaving?

35:54.858 --> 35:55.888
What?

35:56.289 --> 35:57.959
No, no, no.

35:57.994 --> 35:59.565
I'm gonna...

35:59.601 --> 36:00.761
make you lunch.

36:01.968 --> 36:03.229
What are you in the mood for?

36:03.265 --> 36:04.798
A bologna sandwich?

36:05.473 --> 36:06.534
Okay.

36:06.570 --> 36:09.038
But you said you needed
to get out of this place

36:09.073 --> 36:10.134
on the phone just now.

36:10.170 --> 36:11.643
No.

36:11.679 --> 36:12.872
You misheard me.

36:15.214 --> 36:17.448
One bologna sandwich
coming right up.

36:20.083 --> 36:22.150
So how was, uh...

36:22.186 --> 36:23.615
how was school this week?

36:23.651 --> 36:27.192
Learn anything fun
or interesting?

36:27.227 --> 36:30.329
It's school.
It's not fun or interesting.

36:31.028 --> 36:33.097
What about boys?

36:33.132 --> 36:34.759
-(EXCLAIMS)
-Got any crushes?

36:34.795 --> 36:37.130
Ew, no. Why would you even
ask me that?

36:37.165 --> 36:38.937
I am just...

36:38.973 --> 36:40.537
trying to make
some small talk.

36:41.576 --> 36:43.006
Forget it.

36:43.041 --> 36:44.343
I'm not hungry anyway.

36:47.075 --> 36:48.545
Okay.

36:52.516 --> 36:54.413
You don't have to be
my friend, you know.

36:54.449 --> 36:56.151
It's not part of your job.

36:56.186 --> 36:58.017
Well, I'd like to be.

36:58.053 --> 36:59.417
Why?

36:59.452 --> 37:01.187
'Cause I like you.

37:01.223 --> 37:02.559
No, you don't.

37:06.199 --> 37:07.633
CECE: "Do you want juice
 or water?"

37:07.669 --> 37:08.997
"Juice, please."

37:09.033 --> 37:10.231
"Don't spill.

37:10.266 --> 37:11.698
"Juice is a privilege."

37:11.733 --> 37:14.034
"I won't."
"Did you go to the salon today?"

37:14.069 --> 37:15.368
"Yes."

37:15.403 --> 37:16.571
"You look very nice."

37:16.606 --> 37:19.177
-"Thank you."
-Cece, would you like some

37:19.212 --> 37:20.808
dinosaur chicken nuggets
and ketchup?

37:21.442 --> 37:22.912
Ketchup makes a mess.

37:22.948 --> 37:24.309
Yes, it does.

37:24.344 --> 37:25.582
(CECE SIGHS)

37:26.050 --> 37:27.452
(MILLIE SIGHS)

37:31.290 --> 37:33.326
Cece, where did you find
this troll?

37:34.994 --> 37:36.723
Were you in my room?

37:36.758 --> 37:39.124
Cece, this troll is
very special to me.

37:39.159 --> 37:41.396
I don't want you going into
my room, do you understand?

37:41.432 --> 37:43.265
You need to stay
out of the attic.

37:43.300 --> 37:45.400
-So do you.
-(DOOR BANGING)

37:45.436 --> 37:47.439
-ANDREW: Hey.
-(NINA EXCLAIMING)

37:48.402 --> 37:50.543
(BREATH TREMBLING)

37:50.578 --> 37:51.608
(CRYING)

37:52.879 --> 37:55.376
(SIGHS) Hey, Cece,

37:55.412 --> 37:56.442
can you go play
in your bedroom

37:56.478 --> 37:57.746
for a little bit, please?

38:01.086 --> 38:03.056
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

38:03.091 --> 38:04.289
-What happened?
-(TEAPOT WHISTLING)

38:04.324 --> 38:06.090
ANDREW: Premature
ovarian insufficiency.

38:06.125 --> 38:07.459
We've been trying for years.

38:07.961 --> 38:09.590
At least now we know.

38:09.625 --> 38:11.428
-I'm sorry.
-I've just... (SIGHS)

38:11.463 --> 38:14.233
Man, I've just always wanted
a lot of kids.

38:14.268 --> 38:16.765
Like a... Like a whole
soccer team full.

38:17.967 --> 38:20.103
(CLEARS THROAT) Nina and I
were only children like you.

38:20.138 --> 38:21.270
(CABINET KNOB CLICKS)

38:21.305 --> 38:22.534
Well, at least you have Cece.

38:22.569 --> 38:24.003
Of course, of course.

38:27.344 --> 38:28.942
I know it sounds selfish.

38:30.377 --> 38:32.043
I love Cece.

38:32.078 --> 38:34.446
I've always wanted a child
of my own with Nina.

38:34.482 --> 38:35.881
I didn't realize...

38:35.917 --> 38:40.019
Oh, Cece is...
she's absolutely my daughter.

38:40.854 --> 38:43.357
She's just not
my biological daughter.

38:43.392 --> 38:45.124
You're an amazing dad.

38:45.159 --> 38:47.932
Look, I just really don't know
how she's gonna take this.

38:47.967 --> 38:50.167
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

38:50.202 --> 38:51.767
She's been so fragile lately.

38:53.872 --> 38:57.809
I really don't think that she
can handle the disappointment.

38:57.844 --> 38:58.671
She has you.

38:58.707 --> 39:01.073
I don't think
that I am enough.

39:05.249 --> 39:06.518
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

39:15.261 --> 39:16.527
-(NINA SCREAMING)
-(CLANKS)

39:16.562 --> 39:19.561
NINA: It's not fair!
I did everything I could!

39:19.596 --> 39:21.300
ANDREW: Nina,
it's not your fault.

39:21.335 --> 39:23.431
-(SHATTERING)
-NINA: You wish I was gone.

39:23.466 --> 39:24.696
ANDREW: God! Wait! Nina, no!

39:24.731 --> 39:25.863
-Hello?
-ANDREW: No, no, no!

39:25.899 --> 39:27.704
Andrew, are you...
are you okay?

39:29.204 --> 39:30.707
What?

39:33.506 --> 39:34.675
Oh, my God.

39:34.710 --> 39:37.843
-Andrew, are you okay?
-(CHUCKLING)

39:37.878 --> 39:40.579
What? You overheard
those PTA cunts

39:40.614 --> 39:42.187
saying that I'm crazy?

39:42.223 --> 39:44.485
That I don't deserve
my husband?

39:44.520 --> 39:46.789
That I belong in a nuthouse?

39:47.222 --> 39:48.593
Andrew!

39:54.462 --> 39:56.062
Let go of this.

39:57.866 --> 40:00.333
-Wrap this around your hand.
-Thank you.

40:00.369 --> 40:01.738
Alive and well.

40:14.184 --> 40:15.488
(SPRAYING)

40:18.892 --> 40:19.987
(SPRAYING)

40:27.560 --> 40:28.798
(NINA SIGHS)

40:29.766 --> 40:32.472
I cleaned up
the mess from last night.

40:34.341 --> 40:36.806
Sorry I wasn't honest
about the baby.

40:38.440 --> 40:40.077
I guess I was...

40:40.113 --> 40:41.778
trying to manifest.

40:43.049 --> 40:44.209
Or something.

40:46.682 --> 40:48.381
It's okay, I get it.
(CHUCKLES)

40:48.416 --> 40:52.250
I don't know... (CHUCKLING)
...how I'm gonna
face Andrew's mother.

40:56.489 --> 40:57.761
Anyway,

40:58.697 --> 41:01.033
I realized I need to stop
holding onto things

41:01.068 --> 41:02.895
and just start fresh.

41:02.930 --> 41:05.467
So these are
practically brand-new,

41:05.502 --> 41:07.606
and I want you to have them.

41:09.007 --> 41:10.037
I...

41:10.472 --> 41:11.976
I... I can't.

41:12.012 --> 41:13.105
No, seriously,

41:13.141 --> 41:15.444
these are gonna be thrown
in the bin at Goodwill.

41:15.480 --> 41:17.517
This would look
amazing on you.

41:18.117 --> 41:19.783
Millie, take it.

41:20.513 --> 41:21.716
Thanks.

41:21.751 --> 41:23.922
Well, Andrew took Cece
to pancakes,

41:23.957 --> 41:27.191
so you don't really have to
worry about breakfast
this morning.

41:27.226 --> 41:29.289
But I do need a favor.

41:29.324 --> 41:32.730
I need you to look into tickets
for a musical called Showdown.

41:33.530 --> 41:36.201
Andrew's been dying to see it,

41:36.236 --> 41:38.531
and I want to do something to

41:38.566 --> 41:40.540
make it up to him.

41:41.206 --> 41:42.435
Sure. (CHUCKLES)

41:42.471 --> 41:43.840
This Saturday,

41:44.374 --> 41:46.037
if you can manage,

41:46.072 --> 41:49.311
and an overnight
at a high-end hotel.

41:49.347 --> 41:50.444
Splurge on a suite.

41:50.480 --> 41:52.648
Something romantic.

41:52.683 --> 41:55.417
And Cece will be
at a friend's house.

41:55.453 --> 41:57.051
I'll arrange for her to...

41:58.356 --> 41:59.590
uh, be out of the house

41:59.626 --> 42:02.320
and you can just have
the weekend to yourself.

42:03.063 --> 42:05.064
That sounds great.

42:05.099 --> 42:06.858
I'll see what I can do.

42:06.893 --> 42:08.898
You're a lifesaver, Millie.

42:10.668 --> 42:12.869
I don't know
what I'd do without you.

42:13.271 --> 42:14.568
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

42:14.603 --> 42:18.611
(PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)

42:19.573 --> 42:20.943
(EXHALES)

42:24.583 --> 42:26.911
You're with
the Winchesters, right?

42:26.947 --> 42:29.622
-Yeah.
-I'm with the Leightons.

42:30.858 --> 42:32.022
Suzanne?

42:32.057 --> 42:33.120
Right.

42:34.327 --> 42:37.058
Cece's not that good, is she?

42:38.096 --> 42:39.629
(LAUGHS)

42:39.665 --> 42:42.193
Don't worry.
No one gives her any shit.

42:42.228 --> 42:44.362
Not after everything
she's been through.

42:45.765 --> 42:47.200
What do you mean?

42:47.568 --> 42:48.635
Seriously?

42:48.670 --> 42:50.774
All the psycho mom shit?

42:50.810 --> 42:53.338
I know she spent some time
in a psych ward, but...

42:56.114 --> 42:57.144
Um...

42:59.819 --> 43:04.019
Nina Winchester tried
to drown her kid in a bathtub.

43:04.751 --> 43:05.953
-What?
-Yeah.

43:05.988 --> 43:08.490
It's like all the PTA bitches
talk about.

43:08.525 --> 43:10.595
When Cece was a baby,

43:10.630 --> 43:13.561
Nina threw her
in a tub of running water,

43:13.597 --> 43:14.862
then tried to off herself

43:14.897 --> 43:17.128
by swallowing
a shit ton of pills.

43:17.163 --> 43:19.471
Luckily, her husband got
freaked out

43:19.506 --> 43:21.001
when he couldn't get
ahold of her,

43:21.037 --> 43:23.968
then called the police
for a wellness check.

43:24.003 --> 43:27.876
It's, like, fucked up, right?

43:27.911 --> 43:30.813
INSTRUCTOR: Great job,
dancers. Thank you.

43:30.849 --> 43:33.279
-Let's get our belongings.
-GIRL: All right.

43:37.617 --> 43:39.186
(SIGHS)

43:44.862 --> 43:47.392
-Your car smells like feet.
-Thank you.

43:52.203 --> 43:53.233
Hey.

43:55.036 --> 43:57.274
What do you know
about this family?

43:57.309 --> 43:58.439
Sorry, no English.

43:58.475 --> 43:59.844
Oh, bullshit.

44:01.843 --> 44:03.413
I know you shouldn't be here.

44:03.448 --> 44:06.081
-(DOOR OPENS)
-Why?

44:07.287 --> 44:08.383
NINA: Leave him alone.

44:08.419 --> 44:09.447
(DOOR CLOSES)

44:11.558 --> 44:13.858
You've no business
talking to Enzo.

44:14.624 --> 44:17.224
(SCOFFS) What is this?

44:17.260 --> 44:20.232
They're the Broadway tickets
and the hotel reservation.

44:20.267 --> 44:22.028
-For Saturday?
-Yeah.

44:22.063 --> 44:25.232
But why would I have you
book tickets...

44:25.268 --> 44:28.103
for the day that I'm driving
Cece to arts camp in D.C.?

44:28.138 --> 44:30.669
-Why would I do that?
-I don't know, but you did.

44:30.705 --> 44:32.505
No, I didn't.

44:32.540 --> 44:36.174
And I assume that these
are non-refundable now,
at this point?

44:36.209 --> 44:38.409
Nina, I did
what you asked me to do.

44:38.444 --> 44:40.412
Fine. They're gonna
come out of your paycheck.

44:40.447 --> 44:42.587
And I'm so sorry about that,
but it was your mistake,

44:42.622 --> 44:44.520
and you're gonna have to cover
the fee.

44:44.556 --> 44:46.190
Nina, I can't afford that.

44:46.226 --> 44:47.219
I don't care!

44:47.254 --> 44:48.824
It was your mistake.
You're gonna cover it.

44:48.859 --> 44:50.896
Nina, that's more
than I have saved.

44:50.932 --> 44:52.560
Hey.

44:52.596 --> 44:54.030
-Hello.
-NINA: Hi.

44:57.571 --> 44:58.969
Just about
cleaned out the florist,

44:59.005 --> 45:01.741
so otherwise I would have...
I would have got you more.

45:02.407 --> 45:03.743
What's wrong?

45:04.443 --> 45:05.775
Millie booked tickets

45:05.810 --> 45:07.939
for a non-refundable weekend
for us

45:07.974 --> 45:10.781
that we can't even use.

45:10.816 --> 45:12.978
And she's gonna have
to pay for it. Sorry.

45:13.013 --> 45:14.513
No, she doesn't.
That's okay.

45:14.549 --> 45:16.454
We'll just call the credit card
company and have it reversed.

45:16.489 --> 45:17.721
I don't think that's a thing.

45:17.756 --> 45:19.954
ANDREW: That is a thing.
That's a thing.

45:19.989 --> 45:22.157
You don't have to pay
for anything.

45:22.525 --> 45:23.796
Thank you.

45:24.329 --> 45:25.831
I'm sorry.

45:30.202 --> 45:31.298
(SIGHS)

45:34.372 --> 45:35.500
Sweetheart?

45:43.381 --> 45:45.045
(SOFT THUDS)

45:45.080 --> 45:46.517
ANDREW: All this stuff
for a week?

45:46.553 --> 45:48.920
I don't want her
to get homesick.

45:51.852 --> 45:53.353
(ENGINE STARTS)

45:55.823 --> 45:59.095
(WATER RUNNING)

46:15.745 --> 46:18.213
Okay. Sorry. Shit. Okay.

46:18.580 --> 46:19.852
Sorry.

46:27.357 --> 46:30.488
I am so sorry. I usually get
dressed before I come out.

46:30.524 --> 46:33.325
No, it's really my fault.
I was actually just...

46:33.360 --> 46:35.967
I was coming
to confess something to you.

46:37.666 --> 46:41.269
I wanted to let you know
that I couldn't get
the tickets refunded.

46:42.001 --> 46:43.909
-Shit.
-Yeah.

46:46.976 --> 46:49.647
So I think
you should take them

46:49.683 --> 46:51.410
and go to the show
with a friend

46:51.446 --> 46:53.851
and stay in the room,
charge whatever you want.

46:53.887 --> 46:56.482
Room service.
I want you to enjoy yourself.

46:57.389 --> 46:58.918
That is...

46:58.954 --> 47:01.826
really nice of you, but...

47:01.861 --> 47:04.363
I can't. I don't have anyone
I can bring.

47:04.398 --> 47:06.294
You gotta have somebody.

47:08.161 --> 47:10.067
I wish I did, but I don't.

47:11.239 --> 47:12.564
(ANDREW SIGHS)

47:16.074 --> 47:19.142
Okay, well, just, um...
how about you and I go?

47:20.208 --> 47:22.981
We can come back tonight.
I can...

47:23.915 --> 47:25.213
I can sweeten the deal
a little bit,

47:25.249 --> 47:28.283
throw in a slice of pizza,
maybe a hot apple cider?

47:28.951 --> 47:31.121
I'll just tell Nina that I...

47:31.156 --> 47:33.492
exchanged the tickets
and I can take her next week.

47:33.527 --> 47:35.453
No, I can't have you do that.

47:35.488 --> 47:37.726
Oh, come on, we could both
use a night out.

47:37.761 --> 47:40.392
I know we could.
Why not?

47:40.427 --> 47:42.968
I mean, it's supposed to be
a great show.

47:44.600 --> 47:45.663
Okay.

47:46.902 --> 47:49.106
Great. We're going.

47:51.712 --> 47:54.005
(CINNAMON GIRL BY LANA DEL REY
PLAYING)

47:54.041 --> 47:55.607
♪ Cinnamon ♪

47:57.814 --> 47:59.985
♪ In my teeth ♪

48:01.181 --> 48:03.516
♪ From your kiss ♪

48:04.591 --> 48:07.391
♪ You're touching me ♪

48:07.426 --> 48:08.691
Great dress.

48:08.727 --> 48:10.930
♪ All the pills ♪

48:11.697 --> 48:14.130
♪ That you take ♪

48:14.166 --> 48:17.670
♪ Violet, blue, green
 red to keep me ♪

48:17.705 --> 48:21.167
♪ At arm's length don't work ♪

48:21.202 --> 48:23.741
♪ You try to push me out ♪

48:23.776 --> 48:25.575
♪ But I just find my... ♪

48:25.610 --> 48:27.871
Thanks for coming.

48:27.907 --> 48:33.215
♪ Violet, blue, green, red
 to keep me out, I win ♪

48:33.250 --> 48:36.755
♪ There's things
 I wanna say to you ♪

48:36.790 --> 48:39.585
♪ But I'll just let you live ♪

48:39.620 --> 48:43.324
♪ Like if you hold me
 without hurting me ♪

48:43.359 --> 48:46.899
♪ You'll be the first
 who ever did ♪

48:46.934 --> 48:50.394
♪ There's things
 I wanna talk about ♪

48:50.429 --> 48:53.566
♪ But better not to give ♪

48:53.601 --> 48:57.470
♪ But if you hold me
 without hurting me ♪

48:57.505 --> 49:01.376
♪ You'll be the first
 who ever did ♪

49:08.514 --> 49:11.452
♪ Be the first who ever did ♪

49:12.792 --> 49:14.188
-I'm hungry.
-Yeah, I'm hungry.

49:14.224 --> 49:16.420
-I could eat. Yeah.
-Yeah? (CHUCKLES)

49:16.456 --> 49:18.123
Wasn't pizza
a part of this deal?

49:18.158 --> 49:19.690
-Yeah, it was.
-Yeah?

49:19.726 --> 49:23.230
Yeah. You know what?
I think I got a better idea.

49:23.265 --> 49:24.864
MILLIE: Holy shit,
that was amazing.

49:24.900 --> 49:26.033
(ANDREW SIGHS)

49:26.068 --> 49:27.537
-It was, wasn't it?
-Yeah.

49:27.573 --> 49:28.634
ANDREW: Yeah.

49:29.909 --> 49:32.136
MILLIE: This place is
really fancy.

49:32.172 --> 49:33.877
Well, it's charming,

49:33.912 --> 49:35.544
in an old New York
kind of way.

49:35.579 --> 49:36.942
Yeah.

49:36.978 --> 49:38.347
I... I don't...

49:38.382 --> 49:40.051
(CHUCKLING) I don't really
know what I should order.

49:40.086 --> 49:41.950
Well, how about we just get
one of everything?

49:41.985 --> 49:43.218
-Everything?
-Everything.

49:43.254 --> 49:46.124
-(CHUCKLING) We can't do that.
-Yeah, we can.

49:49.089 --> 49:50.458
You like martinis?

49:51.026 --> 49:52.193
I guess. I don't know.

49:52.228 --> 49:54.092
-Well, I guess we'll find out.
-Yeah.

49:54.127 --> 49:55.498
To new adventures.

49:55.533 --> 49:56.629
Cheers.

50:01.534 --> 50:02.874
ANDREW: I mean,
you're funny, you're...

50:02.909 --> 50:04.374
you're caring,
you're great with kids.

50:04.409 --> 50:06.439
I just don't understand why
you're cleaning people's houses.

50:06.475 --> 50:09.012
You should be out there
living your best life.

50:09.047 --> 50:10.608
And have you ever thought
about what

50:10.644 --> 50:13.646
you want to do with your time
on this Earth?

50:14.515 --> 50:17.782
-I don't know. No, not really.
-Why not?

50:18.624 --> 50:19.952
(MILLIE INHALES)

50:19.988 --> 50:21.084
What about you?

50:21.120 --> 50:22.419
Are you...

50:22.454 --> 50:25.191
living your best life doing...

50:25.226 --> 50:27.094
I don't even know what you do.

50:27.129 --> 50:28.798
I run a data processing company

50:28.833 --> 50:30.869
that my father left me.

50:30.904 --> 50:32.901
Basically, I get paid
a lot of money

50:32.937 --> 50:35.305
to do really boring shit.

50:35.340 --> 50:38.075
-Gotcha.
-I mean, all I've ever
really wanted to do

50:38.110 --> 50:40.706
was to be a husband
and a father, honestly.

50:41.241 --> 50:43.045
That's really sweet.

50:43.081 --> 50:45.381
What about you?
Do you want kids?

50:46.452 --> 50:47.515
Yeah.

50:48.014 --> 50:49.253
Someday.

50:50.253 --> 50:52.190
With the right person,
of course.

50:52.724 --> 50:53.951
I mean, I... I...

50:53.986 --> 50:56.225
feel like I won the lottery
with Nina, and I should feel

50:56.261 --> 50:58.727
-like I'm living my best life.
-But you're not?

50:58.763 --> 51:00.432
I love my wife.

51:00.467 --> 51:02.165
I really do.

51:02.200 --> 51:04.229
I just feel like
she's angry all the time,

51:04.264 --> 51:05.699
and I don't know why.

51:05.734 --> 51:08.536
I feel like every conversation
we have ends in a tirade.

51:09.539 --> 51:12.408
If it makes you feel
any better, same. (CHUCKLES)

51:12.443 --> 51:15.646
I mean, she used to be
so different. She was, uh...

51:15.681 --> 51:17.444
She was... loving,

51:17.479 --> 51:19.745
and she was kind,
and she was generous.

51:20.346 --> 51:22.086
She was affectionate.

51:22.121 --> 51:24.789
I mean, all I want to do is
make her happy

51:24.825 --> 51:26.724
and I genuinely
don't know how.

51:26.759 --> 51:28.424
Andrew, it's not you.

51:29.623 --> 51:31.560
I should not have said that.
I'm sorry.

51:31.595 --> 51:33.190
No, it's okay. I mean, I see
the way that she treats you,

51:33.226 --> 51:34.892
and I hate it.

51:36.800 --> 51:37.862
I hate it.

51:39.467 --> 51:41.734
I feel like
I'm letting you down.

51:42.476 --> 51:43.505
You're not.

51:49.082 --> 51:51.315
Pretty sure there's
a dance floor in there.

51:53.751 --> 51:54.745
(CHUCKLES)

51:54.780 --> 51:57.115
-You want to go dancing?
-Should we hit it?

51:57.150 --> 51:58.720
(CHUCKLING)

51:58.755 --> 51:59.818
Yeah.

52:01.121 --> 52:02.357
Let's dance.

52:02.392 --> 52:07.364
♪ Will your eyes
 return to mine? ♪

52:09.168 --> 52:13.205
♪ Will our day start
 to shine? ♪

52:13.873 --> 52:15.701
♪ It was winter ♪

52:15.736 --> 52:22.781
♪ Now let's move
 right into spring ♪

52:22.816 --> 52:26.416
♪ Let the birds sing ♪

52:29.656 --> 52:31.590
(FAINT CLAPPING)

52:31.625 --> 52:33.192
(ANDREW CHUCKLES)

52:34.558 --> 52:37.889
I don't suppose you feel sober
enough to drive us home?

52:38.995 --> 52:40.496
Not really, no.

52:41.494 --> 52:42.927
I think we got a problem.

52:46.633 --> 52:50.407
RECEPTIONIST:
And you're all set.

52:50.442 --> 52:52.370
They're not adjoining,
but they're on the same floor.

52:52.405 --> 52:54.779
-Thanks.
-ANDREW: Mm.

52:54.814 --> 52:55.908
Shit, my phone's dead.

52:55.944 --> 52:57.249
Oh.

52:58.214 --> 52:59.513
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

52:59.548 --> 53:02.247
-Of course. Have a great stay.
-Thank you.

53:02.282 --> 53:04.355
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

53:06.825 --> 53:08.392
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

53:30.147 --> 53:31.811
I'll see you in the morning.

53:33.884 --> 53:35.287
Good night.

53:51.703 --> 53:52.799
(SIGHS)

53:53.573 --> 53:54.603
(SIGHS)

53:58.908 --> 53:59.938
(SIGHS)

54:01.715 --> 54:03.282
(WATER RUNNING)

54:09.153 --> 54:11.648
Do not blow up your life.

54:11.683 --> 54:14.088
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)
-(SIGHS)

54:14.123 --> 54:15.888
(PHONE VIBRATING)

54:22.867 --> 54:24.064
Oh, shit.

54:24.100 --> 54:26.338
(THUNDERCLAP)

54:27.101 --> 54:28.406
(GASPS)

54:28.839 --> 54:30.172
Oh, no.

54:30.207 --> 54:32.839
-(KNOCKING AT DOOR)
-Hey.

54:33.747 --> 54:34.973
What's wrong?

54:39.516 --> 54:41.385
She doesn't mean it.
I'll talk to her.

54:41.421 --> 54:43.684
-She does, Andrew. She does.
-Millie, come here.

54:43.719 --> 54:45.351
(VOICE SHAKING) She wants
to destroy my life,

54:45.386 --> 54:46.652
and I don't know why.

54:46.687 --> 54:49.392
No, she doesn't.
I will talk to her.

54:49.428 --> 54:51.862
Andrew, I know you think
that I can do better,

54:51.898 --> 54:53.662
but I need this job.

54:53.697 --> 54:56.497
I can't lose it. I... I...
I do not want to go back.

54:56.532 --> 55:00.302
-Go back where?
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)

55:00.338 --> 55:01.732
You're not going
to lose your job.

55:01.768 --> 55:03.804
Everything is going
to be okay.

55:04.670 --> 55:06.611
-I promise you.
-(SNIFFLES)

55:06.646 --> 55:07.841
Okay?

55:09.212 --> 55:11.783
Don't cry. It's okay.

55:11.819 --> 55:12.948
It's gonna be okay.

55:12.984 --> 55:14.386
(MILLIE SIGHS)

55:15.052 --> 55:16.452
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

55:16.487 --> 55:17.751
(BAD AS THE REST BY
JESSIE MURPH PLAYING)

55:17.786 --> 55:20.291
♪ Fool me once
 and it's "So what?" ♪

55:20.326 --> 55:22.759
♪ Fool me twice
 I'm a dumb fuck ♪

55:22.794 --> 55:26.292
♪ Three times, you like
 every damn boy I ever loved ♪

55:26.327 --> 55:27.659
♪ Oh, no ♪

55:27.695 --> 55:29.831
(MILLIE MOANS)
Take off my dress.

55:29.866 --> 55:32.437
♪ You're telling me
 that you're the exception ♪

55:32.472 --> 55:34.498
♪ If you a good boy
 with bad intentions ♪

55:34.533 --> 55:35.841
(ZIPPER UNZIPPING)

55:35.876 --> 55:38.340
♪ Tell me now ♪

55:38.375 --> 55:40.539
♪ 'Cause it's kinda late ♪

55:40.574 --> 55:43.214
♪ And I'm emotionally ♪

55:43.249 --> 55:47.044
♪ Kinda twisted right around ♪

55:47.079 --> 55:49.518
♪ And if I stay
 another minute, babe ♪

55:49.553 --> 55:52.083
♪ I'll say a thing
 I never say ♪

55:52.119 --> 55:55.819
♪ 'Cause something
 'bout you breaks me down ♪

55:55.854 --> 56:00.696
♪ I do not love you yet ♪

56:00.731 --> 56:05.598
♪ But I'm 'bout
 as close as I can get ♪

56:05.633 --> 56:08.270
♪ Keep one last percent ♪

56:08.305 --> 56:10.607
♪ Close to my chest ♪

56:10.642 --> 56:15.673
♪ Just in case
you turn out bad as the rest ♪

56:15.708 --> 56:20.277
♪ I will not be a fool ♪

56:20.312 --> 56:25.519
♪ But for you, I might do
 what dumb bitches do ♪

56:25.555 --> 56:27.957
♪ Put on the dress say... ♪

56:27.993 --> 56:29.791
(MOANS SOFTLY)

56:30.391 --> 56:31.924
(THUNDERCLAP)

56:31.960 --> 56:34.693
♪ ...heart
 from my place to your bed ♪

56:34.728 --> 56:38.470
♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪

56:38.938 --> 56:40.835
(THUNDERCLAP)

56:45.145 --> 56:50.944
♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪

56:59.121 --> 57:00.789
(SIGHS)

57:02.656 --> 57:04.188
Nina's coming home early.

57:05.560 --> 57:07.224
So we have to beat her home.

57:09.233 --> 57:10.568
We should get going.

57:11.135 --> 57:12.636
-Okay.
-Okay?

57:14.472 --> 57:16.070
This is gonna sound
really cheesy,

57:16.106 --> 57:19.775
but I didn't think anybody
could look so beautiful
in the morning.

57:29.748 --> 57:31.523
Nina can't ever know.

57:32.688 --> 57:35.359
And this can't
ever happen again.

57:35.394 --> 57:37.595
I really wish
things were different.

57:38.826 --> 57:41.258
I wish I would have
met you before.

57:42.736 --> 57:43.766
Me too.

57:44.300 --> 57:45.537
Are you okay?

57:46.003 --> 57:47.132
Yeah.

57:52.240 --> 57:53.677
(SIGHS)

58:16.396 --> 58:17.899
Nina?

58:23.106 --> 58:24.235
Nina!

58:26.113 --> 58:29.108
I'm gonna go get changed.

58:29.143 --> 58:32.111
I'll start making lunch
just in case she comes back.

58:49.969 --> 58:51.801
Ah, fuck it.

59:17.226 --> 59:18.256
Hello?

59:21.067 --> 59:22.128
Anybody home?

59:25.202 --> 59:26.330
(OVEN DINGS)

59:27.368 --> 59:28.739
Hi.

59:29.405 --> 59:31.442
Welcome home.

59:31.477 --> 59:34.272
-Thank you.
-Lunch is almost ready.

59:34.914 --> 59:36.780
Oh, boy.

59:37.316 --> 59:39.783
-Hi.
-Hey, sweetheart.

59:39.818 --> 59:42.819
-Hi. What are you doing?
-I was just fixing the drain

59:42.854 --> 59:45.421
in the upstairs guest bathroom.
It's a bit clogged.

59:45.457 --> 59:46.887
I knew you would
try to do that.

59:46.922 --> 59:48.351
I said the plumber's coming
on Tuesday.

59:48.387 --> 59:50.292
No, I know. I was just
feeling extra manly today.

59:50.327 --> 59:52.428
-Okay.
-Yeah.

59:52.463 --> 59:54.064
How was the trip? How's Cece?

59:54.099 --> 59:55.700
She's good.

59:57.035 --> 59:58.732
Listen.

59:58.768 --> 01:00:00.672
I'm very sorry
about last night.

01:00:01.670 --> 01:00:03.340
It was a very long drive.

01:00:03.375 --> 01:00:04.770
I was very tired. (CHUCKLES)

01:00:04.805 --> 01:00:07.043
I do not sleep well in hotels,

01:00:07.079 --> 01:00:08.106
turns out.

01:00:08.142 --> 01:00:10.745
And I should not be left alone
with my phone.

01:00:10.780 --> 01:00:14.344
So, lesson learned.
It's a new day.

01:00:14.379 --> 01:00:16.982
-Please accept my apologies.
-Yeah, it's okay.

01:00:17.018 --> 01:00:18.984
-I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
-It's okay.

01:00:19.020 --> 01:00:21.158
-(EXHALES)
-Let's get some food in ya.

01:00:21.193 --> 01:00:22.086
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

01:00:22.121 --> 01:00:24.729
-NINA: Mm. Mm.
-NINA AND ANDREW: Hi.

01:00:25.530 --> 01:00:27.666
-This looks fantastic.
-Yes.

01:00:29.399 --> 01:00:31.466
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

01:00:31.502 --> 01:00:33.471
...you know? Hey, Millie.

01:00:33.506 --> 01:00:36.169
-MILLIE: Mm-hmm.
-How was your night off?

01:00:37.575 --> 01:00:40.036
Uh, my best friend Lexi
took me

01:00:40.072 --> 01:00:42.439
-to Peter Luger.
-ANDREW: Hmm.

01:00:42.474 --> 01:00:44.644
Um, she had a gift certificate.
It was really nice.

01:00:44.679 --> 01:00:46.445
We had a lot of sides.

01:00:46.481 --> 01:00:47.681
(CHUCKLES)

01:00:47.716 --> 01:00:49.652
But I don't really eat meat.

01:00:49.687 --> 01:00:51.952
This looks incredible.
So, thank you.

01:00:51.988 --> 01:00:55.623
I don't know why
but my quiches never turn out.

01:00:55.658 --> 01:00:57.025
I've been meaning to ask you.

01:00:57.060 --> 01:00:59.329
Did you learn how to cook
while you were in prison?

01:00:59.364 --> 01:01:00.424
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:01:02.195 --> 01:01:03.995
You know, she was in prison
for ten years

01:01:04.031 --> 01:01:06.034
before she came to
work with us.

01:01:07.105 --> 01:01:08.366
Right?

01:01:09.440 --> 01:01:10.775
I think it's brave,

01:01:11.643 --> 01:01:15.141
making a new start
in a new town.

01:01:15.177 --> 01:01:18.343
I'm glad that we could be
a part of your journey.

01:01:20.317 --> 01:01:21.445
(NINA SIPS)

01:01:24.320 --> 01:01:26.250
Oh.

01:01:26.286 --> 01:01:28.853
We need a restock
of all of Cece's favorites

01:01:28.888 --> 01:01:30.122
before she gets home.

01:01:30.158 --> 01:01:32.423
You haven't really been
keeping up with that.

01:01:33.266 --> 01:01:35.859
And could you... Sorry.

01:01:35.895 --> 01:01:36.929
Could you use my car

01:01:36.965 --> 01:01:38.196
for running errands
from now on

01:01:38.232 --> 01:01:39.700
until you can save up
to get something nicer?

01:01:39.735 --> 01:01:41.739
I'm afraid yours is becoming

01:01:41.775 --> 01:01:44.468
an unwelcome topic
of conversation. Here you go.

01:01:45.643 --> 01:01:47.240
-You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

01:01:47.840 --> 01:01:50.045
(SIGHS) You okay?

01:01:51.545 --> 01:01:53.015
Yeah.

01:01:56.620 --> 01:01:58.215
MILLIE: I had it all wrong.

01:01:58.250 --> 01:01:59.917
 Nina was never
 one of those women

01:01:59.953 --> 01:02:01.389
 just going with her gut.

01:02:01.424 --> 01:02:02.524
 She knew.

01:02:02.559 --> 01:02:03.894
 The whole fucking time,

01:02:03.929 --> 01:02:06.092
 she knew I needed this job
 and couldn't leave,

01:02:06.127 --> 01:02:08.931
 no matter how shitty
 she made my life.

01:02:08.967 --> 01:02:11.330
 What kind of bitch
 does something like that?

01:02:12.934 --> 01:02:15.037
CASHIER: Thanks,
have a good day.

01:02:17.408 --> 01:02:19.136
Hello, Millie.

01:02:19.171 --> 01:02:21.877
-Hi.
-Is that the newest phone?

01:02:21.912 --> 01:02:24.446
What do you think
of that camera? It's...

01:02:24.482 --> 01:02:26.177
pretty great, right?

01:02:26.212 --> 01:02:28.246
I wouldn't know.
I only use it for work.

01:02:28.281 --> 01:02:31.086
Well, still, you're very
trusting. (CHUCKLES)

01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:32.922
What do you mean?

01:02:32.958 --> 01:02:35.626
Pumpkin, most of the nannies
won't take the phone

01:02:35.661 --> 01:02:37.354
'cause they don't want
every text,

01:02:37.389 --> 01:02:40.027
every call,
every place you go tracked.

01:02:40.062 --> 01:02:42.727
But, I mean,
you have nothing to hide, so...

01:02:42.763 --> 01:02:44.033
good for you.

01:02:45.166 --> 01:02:47.405
MILLIE: And that's
 when I realized

01:02:47.440 --> 01:02:49.170
 that Nina knew everything.

01:02:51.036 --> 01:02:52.371
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:02:56.275 --> 01:02:58.746
-OFFICER: Millie Calloway.
-Yeah?

01:02:58.781 --> 01:03:00.513
Hands against the car, please.

01:03:00.549 --> 01:03:01.848
What? Why?

01:03:01.884 --> 01:03:03.518
I said,
"Hands against the car."

01:03:03.553 --> 01:03:04.917
Ow! What did I do?

01:03:04.953 --> 01:03:07.250
This car's been
reported stolen.

01:03:07.286 --> 01:03:08.557
-What? No.
-(HANDCUFFS RATCHETING)

01:03:08.593 --> 01:03:10.290
No, this is my boss's car.

01:03:11.164 --> 01:03:12.259
(RATCHETING)

01:03:18.469 --> 01:03:20.897
(BREATH TREMBLING)

01:03:20.933 --> 01:03:22.401
(SIREN CHIRPS)

01:03:40.987 --> 01:03:43.191
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

01:03:43.824 --> 01:03:45.088
ANDREW: Thank you.

01:03:45.124 --> 01:03:47.932
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

01:03:56.176 --> 01:03:57.337
I'm sorry.

01:04:01.541 --> 01:04:05.312
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
the truth about prison.

